<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE starlink-15-18 ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Falcon 9 Starlink Group 15-18 (27 V2 Mini Optimized, SLC-4E) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
TIMELINE mode: every ignition/cutoff/separation/fairing time is a published hard event; mdot=F_vac/(Isp_vac*g0); thrust SL/vac on ambient pressure.
FITTED (least squares vs published knots): vertical rise 9.59 s, kick 3.459 deg over 10 s, Cd 0.400, payload 16767 kg,
gravity turn, then linear-tangent steering tan(theta)=0.5643-0.001406*(t-t_ign stage 1).
Vehicle config: SpaceX Falcon 9 Block 5 (reusable first stage, droneship recovery) — TIMELINE mode (sim/vehicles/falcon9.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
Falcon 9 Block 5 masses from Wikipedia &#x27;Falcon 9 Block 5&#x27; spec table; thrust/Isp from Wikipedia &#x27;Falcon 9&#x27; spec table (citing SpaceX).
TIMELINE mode (tuned 2026-10-25): MECO 146 s, stage sep 150 s, SES-1 156 s, fairing 176 s, SECO-1 (final cutoff) from SpaceX&#x27;s sl-15-16 timeline are hard events.
Throttle profile not published: full published thrust throughout; unburned stage-1 residual stands in for entry/landing propellant.
Not flown: LL2 NET 2026-10-31T03:48:00Z (Fri Oct 30 8:48 pm PDT), status Go (LL2 checked 2026-10-29 ~8:10a PDT); SpaceX launches page Oct 30 23:48 ET agrees; NAVAREA XII 747/26 window 310348Z-310831Z OCT covers it. Retimed from the earlier T0 2026-10-30T04:02:00Z (Thu Oct 29 9:02 pm PDT); SpaceX timeline unchanged. Spaceflight Now schedule not machine-readable from the box (JS/API-gated). File continues past SECO-1 through SES-2/SECO-2 to payload deploy (POST-CUTOFF lines).
Published timeline (SpaceX sl-15-18): Max-Q 1:08, MECO 2:26, stage sep 2:29, SES-1 2:36, fairing 2:58, SECO-1 8:39, SES-2 53:07, SECO-2 53:08, deploy 1:01:59. Booster: 18th flight (SpaceX), LL2/prior board B1093; OCISLY.
Target orbit: SpaceX pre-launch state vector (CelesTrak SupGP starlink-g15-18): deploy 251 x 266 km, i 70.004 deg. Deploy epoch 2026-10-31T04:51:14Z = T+1:03:14 vs SpaceX page 1:01:59 (75 s, noted).
Target (see launch config): insertion 177 km, apoapsis 266 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 155.80 deg; payload 16767 kg.
Pad: 34.632000N -120.611000E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-10-31T03:48:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF: after final cutoff T+519.0 s the stage coasts (same WGS-84/J2/US76-drag model) to PAYLOAD DEPLOY T+3719 s; rows after cutoff tagged -coast/-burn.
POST-CUTOFF burn &#x27;SES-2/SECO-2 (MVac restart)&#x27;: ign T+3187.0 s, 1.0 s at 517.67 kN prograde (Isp 348 s); timing from SpaceX sl-15-18 timeline; thrust solved (throttle unpublished) so the 1 s burn raises perigee to the SpaceX/CelesTrak deploy perigee 251.1 km.
POST-CUTOFF deploy T+3719 s (SpaceX sl-15-18 timeline: deploy T+01:01:59): alt 265.39 km, osculating 253.6 x 266.3 km, i 69.996 deg.
POST-CUTOFF note: CelesTrak SupGP deploy-state epoch 2026-10-31T04:51:14Z = T+3794 s, 75 s after SpaceX&#x27;s published deploy; SpaceX time used.
POST-CUTOFF note: Perigee/apogee are osculating (r - 6378.137 km) and will differ by a few km from CelesTrak mean elements.</description>
